From 5c8ea19cd6814266410a5d91a5f6019f0dd3db3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "keepup[bot]" <keepup[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat: load the native embedder through
 @huggingface/transformers

@xenova/transformers has had no release since 29 May 2024, and the ONNX
build of EmbeddingGemma 2, whose Hugging Face repo was created on 4 Oct 2026,
targets its maintained successor. Move only the native embedder for now, at
4.3.0, the latest release on that date. The reranker and local Whisper stay
on the old package, so the collector's dependencies do not change.

Every existing model now names dtype "q8": that is the quantized file the
old package loaded by default, so existing downloads keep being used.

The new package's pipeline() drops cache_dir for some of its file lookups,
and those go to the network unless env.cacheDir holds the file. Set it to our
cache, so a downloaded model still loads with Hugging Face unreachable, as it
does on the old package.

server/.yarnrc skips onnxruntime-node's install step. On linux/x64 it
downloads CUDA files from NuGet that the embedder never uses, because it runs
on the CPU, and yarn install fails if NuGet can't be reached.

sharp is pinned to 0.34.5 under the new package. sharp 0.35 requires Node
20.9, and yarn refuses to install it on the Node 18 used by CI and Docker.

Replay date: 4 Oct 2026. Source:
https://huggingface.co/onnx-community/embeddinggemma-2-ONNX
